Title:
VMkatz — Extract Windows credentials directly from VM memory snapshots and virtual disks

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
VMkatz is an offline credential extraction tool that parses virtualization artifacts (VM memory snapshots, saved states, virtual disks, and some backup formats) to recover Windows secrets without needing to boot or access the guest OS. It targets the “too big to steal” problem by extracting high-value data in-place from `.vmsn/.vmem`, `.sav`, `.vmrs`, `.vmdk/.qcow2/.vhdx`, raw VMFS/LVM devices, registry hives, and LSASS minidumps. The tool implements mimikatz-style LSASS parsing to extract credentials from multiple SSP providers (e.g., MSV, Kerberos, WDigest, DPAPI, CredMan, CloudAP) and can also recover BitLocker FVEKs from memory. From disks it supports SAM/LSA/DCC2 extraction, DPAPI masterkeys (hashcat-ready), and full NTDS.dit parsing via a native ESE parser for domain controller disks. It’s primarily useful for red teams and post-exploitation operators operating near hypervisors/NAS/backup repos, and also for DFIR analysts needing repeatable offline extraction across many VM artifacts. Notable is its broad hypervisor/format coverage, static small binary footprint, and focus on robust parsing (paging/EPT translation, carve mode for truncated dumps, and ticket export).

Technical Focus:
- Offline LSASS credential extraction (SSP provider structures, linked lists/AVL trees)
- Virtual memory translation (page tables, EPT scanning, pagefile resolution)
- Offline Windows secrets from disk (SAM, SECURITY/SYSTEM, LSA secrets, DCC2)
- NTDS.dit parsing via ESE database parsing and hash extraction
- BitLocker key recovery (FVEK pool tag scanning) and transparent disk decryption
- Offline DPAPI decryption and browser secrets extraction (Chromium/Firefox; App-Bound Encryption)

Use Cases:
- Extract NTLM hashes/Kerberos tickets/DPAPI keys from VM snapshots on ESXi/Proxmox/NAS without exfiltrating full images
- Pull SAM/LSA secrets and cached domain creds from stolen/accessible virtual disks
- Dump AD credential material from domain controller virtual disks (NTDS.dit + SYSTEM)
- Recover BitLocker FVEKs from memory snapshots to decrypt protected volumes offline
- Triage backup repositories (e.g., Veeam) for credential material at scale
- DFIR validation/correlation of credentials across snapshots, disks, and minidumps

Keywords:
VMkatz, LSASS, mimikatz, pypykatz, NTLM, Kerberos, DPAPI, WDigest, MSV1_0, CredMan, CloudAP, TsPkg, LiveSSP, SSP, NTDS.dit, ESE, SAM, LSA secrets, DCC2, BitLocker FVEK, page tables, EPT, pagefile, VMDK, QCOW2, VHDX, VMFS, ESXi, Proxmox, Veeam VBK, Hyper-V VMRS, VirtualBox SAV, minidump, Rust